---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import IssueRow from '../../components/IssueRow.astro';
import { ENGINES, fidelity, fmt, issues, openFidelity, severityRank, url } from '../../lib/data';
import { CLASSES, accepted, acceptedIn, portBugs, skipped } from '../../lib/issues';

const engines = ENGINES.filter((e) => issues.some((i) => i.engine === e)).concat(
	[...new Set(issues.map((i) => i.engine))].filter((e) => !ENGINES.includes(e)),
);
const severities = [...new Set(issues.map((i) => i.severity))].sort((a, b) => severityRank(a) - severityRank(b));
const count = (sev: string, eng: string) => issues.filter((i) => i.severity === sev && i.engine === eng).length;
const twopi = fidelity.layout.find((l) => l.name === 'twopi')!;
const lastFuzz = fidelity.fuzz.rounds[fidelity.fuzz.rounds.length - 1];
const byClass = CLASSES.map((c) => ({ ...c, list: acceptedIn(c.key) }));
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: "What's left", description: 'Open differences between graphviz-pure and C Graphviz 16.1.0: bugs in the port, and C behaviour the port does not or should not reproduce.' }} headings={[{ depth: 2, slug: 'port', text: 'In the port' }, { depth: 2, slug: 'open', text: 'Open fidelity issues' }, { depth: 2, slug: 'accepted', text: 'Accepted differences' }, { depth: 2, slug: 'skipped', text: 'The inputs the full check skips' }, { depth: 2, slug: 'known', text: 'In numbers' }]}>
	<p class="intro">
		Everything known not to match, each with a minimised reproducer, C's output and the port's. <strong>In the port</strong> means the port
		should change. <strong>Accepted differences</strong> means C's output comes from undefined behaviour, a crash path or nondeterminism, so it
		cannot or should not be reproduced byte for byte; the port should still behave sensibly there. Every accepted difference is in one of four
		classes: C nondeterminism or undefined behaviour, a C crash or assertion, C's error path, or the platform libm.
	</p>

	{issues.length > 0 && (
		<table class="ledger matrix">
			<thead><tr><th>Severity</th>{engines.map((e) => <th class="n">{e}</th>)}<th class="n">Total</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				{severities.map((s) => (
					<tr><td>{s}</td>{engines.map((e) => <td class="n">{count(s, e) || '·'}</td>)}<td class="n">{issues.filter((i) => i.severity === s).length}</td></tr>
				))}
			</tbody>
		</table>
	)}

	<h2 id="port">In the port <span class="n">{portBugs.length}</span></h2>
	{portBugs.length ? <ul class="list">{portBugs.map((i) => <IssueRow i={i} />)}</ul> : <p class="empty">No open difference in the port: every case the fuzzing rounds found is fixed or accepted.</p>}

	<h2 id="open">Open fidelity issues <span class="n">{openFidelity.length}</span></h2>
	<p class="intro">
		The issues in the repository that are open and labelled <code>fidelity</code>. A difference in the port that is not listed
		here yet is one the fuzzing rounds have not found.
	</p>
	<ul class="list">
		{openFidelity.map((o) => (
			<li class="irow">
				<span class="sev">issue</span>
				<div class="main">
					<a href={o.url}>#{o.number} — {o.title}</a>
					<span class="sub">{o.note}</span>
				</div>
				<span class="filed"><a href={o.url}>GitHub issue</a></span>
			</li>
		))}
	</ul>

	<h2 id="accepted">Accepted differences <span class="n">{accepted.length}</span></h2>
	{byClass.map((c) => (
		<section>
			<h3 id={`class-${c.key}`}>{c.label} <span class="n">{c.list.length}</span></h3>
			{c.list.length ? <ul class="list">{c.list.map((i) => <IssueRow i={i} />)}</ul> : <p class="empty">None.</p>}
		</section>
	))}

	<h2 id="skipped">The inputs the full check skips <span class="n">{skipped.length}</span></h2>
	<p class="intro">
		The full-pipeline check compares the port's whole <code>-Tsvg</code> with C's, byte for byte, on every corpus input. These
		{skipped.length} inputs it does not compare, because C has no single output for them: C's own output changes from run to run, or C
		crashes. Each one has the same cause as an accepted difference above.
	</p>
	<table class="ledger skips">
		<thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>Class</th><th>Cause</th></tr></thead>
		<tbody>
			{skipped.map((s) => (
				<tr>
					<td class="mono">{s.input}</td>
					<td>{CLASSES.find((c) => c.key === s.class)?.short ?? s.class}</td>
					<td>{s.cause}{s.issue && <> <a href={s.issue}>Issue</a></>}</td>
				</tr>
			))}
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="known">In numbers</h2>
	<ul class="known">
		{fidelity.e2e.differs.length > 0 && <li><strong>{fmt(fidelity.e2e.differs.length)} corpus files differ from C with the same math</strong>: see the <a href={url('fidelity/#full-pipeline')}>file list</a>.</li>}
		<li><strong>{fmt(fidelity.e2e.stock.libm_only)} corpus files differ from stock C on macOS</strong> only because C there calls Apple's libm; the port equals C computing with the same math on each. These are not bugs, by policy: every build uses the same math library and never follows a platform libm (<a href={url('porting/libm/')}>The math library</a>, <a href={url('fidelity/#stock-c-on-macos')}>the file list</a>).</li>
		<li><strong>{twopi.total - twopi.exact} twopi layouts</strong>: C routes the arrows graphs differently from run to run (<a href={url('whats-left/twopi-arrows-c-nondeterministic-routing/')}>issue</a>).</li>
		<li><strong>{(100 - lastFuzz.all).toFixed(1)}% differed in historical fuzzing round {lastFuzz.round}</strong>, before later fixes; the round-by-round record is in <a href={url('porting/fuzzing/')}>the fuzzing notes</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>stderr</strong>: the port prints C's warnings, and so does the wording of DOT syntax errors.</li>
	</ul>
</StarlightPage>

<style>
	.intro { color: var(--key-2); }
	.matrix { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 40rem; }
	h2 .n, h3 .n { font-family: var(--face-mono); font-size: var(--sl-text-sm); font-weight: 400; color: var(--key-3); margin-left: 0.5rem; }
	h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
	.list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; border-top: 0.5px solid var(--rule-strong); }
	.empty { color: var(--key-3); }
	.known li { color: var(--key-2); }
	.known strong { color: var(--key); }
	.known a { color: var(--register); }
	.skips { margin-top: 1rem; }
	.skips td { vertical-align: top; }
	.skips td.mono { font-family: var(--face-mono); font-size: var(--sl-text-xs); white-space: nowrap; }
	.skips a { color: var(--register); }
</style>
